Lei Wang received his B.S. degree from the Fuyang Normal University in 2013. He received his M.S. degree from the Anhui University of Science and Technology in 2017. He received his Ph.D. degrees from the Fudan University in 2021. He is engaged in the magnetic-dielectric synergy microwave absorbers, especially metal-organic frameworks derived functional materials.
Renchao Che received his M.S. degree from Harbin Institute of Technology in in 1997 and his Ph.D. degrees from Chinese Academy of Sciences in 2003, respectively. He is a distinguished researcher at the Fudan University. His research interest includes in-situ electron microscopy, energy materials, semiconductor superlattices and microwave absorbing materials.
